{"title":"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The month of June has 30 days. If in a certain year June 1 is on a Tuesday, on which day of the week is June 30?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2440094769522cc6d9c171cb90fb928e132dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{Monday} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{Tuesday} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{Wednesday} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{Thursday} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{Friday}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"620\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>June 30 would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> days after June 1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85cb8bfcf15c9ae48bcaefebfeb13a13cebe6c52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\times 4 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (the number of days in a week), so June 30 would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> day after a Tuesday, which is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/162c5159d31872b827954957623578195ebfa11e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } \\text{Wednesday}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"129\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /